            "solvedExample": {
                "question": "<p>Water ($\\rho = 1,000\\text{ kg/m}^3$) flows steadily through a horizontal venturi pipe ($z_1 = z_2$). The pipe diameter reduces from $D_1 = 100\\text{ mm}$ ($0.100\\text{ m}$) at the inlet to $D_2 = 50\\text{ mm}$ ($0.050\\text{ m}$) at the throat. The inlet static pressure is $P_1 = 160\\text{ kPa}$ and inlet velocity is $v_1 = 2.0\\text{ m/s}$.</p>\n<p>Assuming frictionless flow, the throat velocity $v_2$ and throat pressure $P_2$ are:</p>\n<div class=\"grid grid-cols-2 gap-2 my-2 font-mono text-xs\">\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(A) $v_2 = 8.0\\text{ m/s}, \\quad P_2 = 130\\text{ kPa}$</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(B) $v_2 = 4.0\\text{ m/s}, \\quad P_2 = 154\\text{ kPa}$</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(C) $v_2 = 8.0\\text{ m/s}, \\quad P_2 = 190\\text{ kPa}$</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(D) $v_2 = 16.0\\text{ m/s}, \\quad P_2 = 100\\text{ kPa}$</div>\n</div>",
                "solution": "<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 1: Continuity Equation for Incompressible Flow</strong></p>\n$$A_1 v_1 = A_2 v_2 \\implies v_2 = v_1 \\left(\\frac{D_1}{D_2}\\right)^2 = (2.0\\text{ m/s}) \\left(\\frac{100\\text{ mm}}{50\\text{ mm}}\\right)^2 = 2.0 \\times 4 = 8.0\\text{ m/s}$$\n<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 2: Apply Bernoulli Equation ($z_1 = z_2$)</strong></p>\n$$P_1 + \\frac{1}{2}\\rho v_1^2 = P_2 + \\frac{1}{2}\\rho v_2^2 \\implies P_2 = P_1 - \\frac{1}{2}\\rho (v_2^2 - v_1^2)$$\n$$P_2 = 160,000\\text{ Pa} - \\frac{1}{2}(1,000\\text{ kg/m}^3)\\left((8.0)^2 - (2.0)^2\\right)$$\n$$P_2 = 160,000 - 500(64 - 4) = 160,000 - 500(60) = 160,000 - 30,000 = 130,000\\text{ Pa} = 130\\text{ kPa}$$\n<p class=\"mt-2 pt-2 border-t border-emerald-500/20\"><strong class=\"text-cyan-300\">Correct Answer:</strong> <span class=\"text-emerald-300 font-bold\">(A) $v_2 = 8.0\\text{ m/s}, \\quad P_2 = 130\\text{ kPa}$</span></p>\n<p class=\"text-[11px] text-slate-400\"><em>FE Exam Tip:</em> As fluid velocity increases in a restriction, static pressure decreases (Venturi effect). This pressure drop $\\Delta P = P_1 - P_2$ is commonly measured to determine pipeline flow rate $Q$.</p>"
            }
