            "solvedExample": {
                "question": "<p>A planar quartz inspection window of an annealing furnace has thickness $L = 12.0\\text{ mm} = 0.0120\\text{ m}$, cross-sectional area $A = 0.400\\text{ m}^2$, and thermal conductivity $k = 1.40\\text{ W/(m}\\cdot\\text{K)}$. The inside surface is at $T_1 = 550.0^\\circ\\text{C}$ and the outside surface is at $T_2 = 150.0^\\circ\\text{C}$.</p>\n<p>From Fourier’s law, the steady rate of conductive heat transfer $\\dot{Q}$ and conduction thermal resistance $R_{\\text{th}}$ are:</p>\n<div class=\"grid grid-cols-2 gap-2 my-2 font-mono text-xs\">\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(A) $\\dot{Q} = 18.67\\text{ kW}, \\quad R_{\\text{th}} = 0.0214\\text{ K/W}$</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(B) $\\dot{Q} = 9.33\\text{ kW}, \\quad R_{\\text{th}} = 0.0429\\text{ K/W}$</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(C) $\\dot{Q} = 37.33\\text{ kW}, \\quad R_{\\text{th}} = 0.0107\\text{ K/W}$</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(D) $\\dot{Q} = 18.67\\text{ kW}, \\quad R_{\\text{th}} = 0.0467\\text{ K/W}$</div>\n</div>",
                "solution": "<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 1: Calculate Conduction Thermal Resistance ($R_{\\text{th}}$)</strong></p>\n$$R_{\\text{th}} = \\frac{L}{k A} = \\frac{0.0120\\text{ m}}{(1.40\\text{ W/(m}\\cdot\\text{K)})(0.400\\text{ m}^2)} = \\frac{0.0120}{0.560} \\approx 0.02143\\text{ K/W}$$\n<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 2: Calculate Steady Heat Transfer Rate ($\\dot{Q}$)</strong></p>\n$$\\dot{Q} = \\frac{T_1 - T_2}{R_{\\text{th}}} = \\frac{550.0^\\circ\\text{C} - 150.0^\\circ\\text{C}}{0.02143\\text{ K/W}} = \\frac{400.0\\text{ K}}{0.02143\\text{ K/W}} \\approx 18{,}667\\text{ W} \\approx 18.67\\text{ kW}$$\n<p class=\"mt-2 pt-2 border-t border-emerald-500/20\"><strong class=\"text-cyan-300\">Correct Answer:</strong> <span class=\"text-emerald-300 font-bold\">(A) $\\dot{Q} = 18.67\\text{ kW}, \\quad R_{\\text{th}} = 0.0214\\text{ K/W}$</span></p>\n<p class=\"text-[11px] text-slate-400\"><em>FE Exam Tip:</em> The temperature difference $\\Delta T = 400.0\\text{ K}$ is identical in Celsius and Kelvin ($1^\\circ\\text{C} = 1\\text{ K}$ temperature interval).</p>"
            }
