                "solution": "<p><strong>Step 1: Calculate Pitch Line Velocity ($v_t$)</strong></p>\n<p>$$\\omega = \\frac{2 \\pi N}{60} = \\frac{2 \\pi (1{,}200)}{60} = 125.66\\text{ rad/s}$$</p>\n<p>$$v_t = \\omega r = (125.66\\text{ rad/s}) \\left(\\frac{0.120\\text{ m}}{2}\\right) = (125.66)(0.060\\text{ m}) = 7.540\\text{ m/s}$$</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2: Calculate Transmitted Tangential Load ($W_t$)</strong></p>\n<p>$$W_t = \\frac{P}{v_t} = \\frac{15{,}000\\text{ W}}{7.540\\text{ m/s}} = 1{,}989.4\\text{ N} \\approx 1{,}989\\text{ N}$$</p>\n<p><strong>Step 3: Calculate Tooth Root Bending Stress ($\\sigma$)</strong></p>\n<p>$$\\sigma = \\frac{W_t}{F m Y} = \\frac{1{,}989.4\\text{ N}}{(0.0400\\text{ m})(0.00400\\text{ m})(0.320)} = \\frac{1{,}989.4\\text{ N}}{5.12 \\times 10^{-5}\\text{ m}^2}$$</p>\n<p>$$\\sigma = 3.8855 \\times 10^7\\text{ Pa} = 38.86\\text{ MPa} \\approx 38.9\\text{ MPa}$$</p>\n<p><strong>Correct Answer:</strong> (A) $W_t = 1{,}989\\text{ N}, \\quad \\sigma = 38.9\\text{ MPa}$</p>\n<p><strong>FE Exam Tip:</strong> In US Customary units, the Lewis formula is $\\sigma = \\frac{W_t P_d}{F Y}$, where $P_d = 1/m$ is the diametral pitch in teeth per inch.</p>"
