            "title": "Concrete Slump Test and Air Entrainment Acceptance Testing",
            "formula": "$$\\text{Slump} = 12\\text{ in} - h_{\\text{slumped}} \\quad (\\text{ASTM C143}); \\quad A = A_1 - G \\quad (\\text{ASTM C231 Pressure Method})$$",
            "description": "Standard field acceptance testing for fresh concrete consistency, workability, and freeze-thaw durability. ASTM C143 slump cone (12-in height, 4-in top, 8-in base) is filled in three equal-volume layers with 25 strokes per layer using a 5/8-in tamping rod. ASTM C231 Type B pressure air meter measures apparent entrained air $A_1$ corrected by aggregate correction factor $G$.",
            "examTip": "Found in Civil: Materials (Concrete). ASTM C143 specifies 3 layers of EQUAL VOLUME (approx 2-5/8 in, 6-1/8 in, and full 12 in depth), NOT equal height. In air content testing, always subtract aggregate correction factor $G$ ($A = A_1 - G$). Target air entrainment for severe freeze-thaw exposure is typically $4.5\\%$ to $7.5\\%$.",
            "isNew": true,
