            "solvedExample": {
                "question": "<p>A reinforced concrete beam is designed with No. 8 longitudinal tension bars ($d_b = 1.000\\text{ in}$) having specified yield strength $f_y = 60{,}000\\text{ psi}$.</p>\n<p>The beam is cast using normal-weight concrete ($\\lambda = 1.0$) with specified compressive strength $f'_c = 4{,}000\\text{ psi}$. The bars are uncoated ($\\psi_e = 1.0$), bottom-cast with less than $12\\text{ in}$ of concrete below ($\\psi_t = 1.0$), and clear spacing/cover satisfy ACI criteria allowing the simplified equation $l_d = \\left(\\frac{f_y \\psi_t \\psi_e}{20 \\lambda \\sqrt{f'_c}}\\right) d_b$.</p>\n<p>The required tension development length $l_d$ is most nearly:</p>\n<div class=\"grid grid-cols-2 gap-2 my-2 font-mono text-xs\">\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(A) $l_d = 36.5\\text{ in}$</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(B) $l_d = 47.4\\text{ in}$</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(C) $l_d = 58.2\\text{ in}$</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(D) $l_d = 65.0\\text{ in}$</div>\n</div>",
                "solution": "<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 1: Calculate Concrete Tensile Resistance Parameter</strong></p>\n$$\\sqrt{f'_c} = \\sqrt{4{,}000\\text{ psi}} = 63.2456\\text{ psi}$$\n<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 2: Evaluate Modification Factors</strong></p>\n$$\\lambda = 1.0, \\quad \\psi_t = 1.0, \\quad \\psi_e = 1.0$$\n<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 3: Calculate Development Length ($l_d$)</strong></p>\n$$l_d = \\left(\\frac{f_y \\psi_t \\psi_e}{20 \\lambda \\sqrt{f'_c}}\\right) d_b = \\left[\\frac{(60{,}000\\text{ psi})(1.0)(1.0)}{20(1.0)(63.2456\\text{ psi})}\\right](1.000\\text{ in})$$\n$$l_d = \\frac{60{,}000}{1264.91} \\times 1.000 = 47.43\\text{ inches} \\approx 47.4\\text{ in}$$\n<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 4: Verify ACI Code Minimum</strong></p>\n$$l_d = 47.43\\text{ in} \\ge 12.0\\text{ in} \\quad (\\text{Satisfied})$$\n<p class=\"mt-2 pt-2 border-t border-emerald-500/20\"><strong class=\"text-cyan-300\">Correct Answer:</strong> <span class=\"text-emerald-300 font-bold\">(B) $l_d = 47.4\\text{ in}$</span></p>\n<p class=\"text-[11px] text-slate-400\"><em>FE Exam Tip:</em> If these were top-cast bars (with $>12\\text{ in}$ of concrete placed below them), $\\psi_t = 1.3$, increasing $l_d$ to $47.43 \\times 1.3 = 61.7\\text{ in}$ due to water bleed accumulation beneath the bar ribs.</p>"
            }
