            "solvedExample": {
                "question": "<p>An unconfined compression test is performed on an undisturbed cylindrical specimen of saturated clay with initial diameter $D_0 = 50.0\\text{ mm}$ and initial length $L_0 = 100.0\\text{ mm}$.</p>\n<p>At compressive failure, the peak axial load measured is $P_{\\max} = 275\\text{ N}$, and the specimen exhibits an axial shortening of $\\Delta L = 8.0\\text{ mm}$.</p>\n<p>Using the strain-corrected cross-sectional area, the unconfined compressive strength ($q_u$), undrained shear strength ($c_u$), and qualitative consistency classification are:</p>\n<div class=\"grid grid-cols-2 gap-2 my-2 font-mono text-xs\">\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(A) $q_u = 70.0\\text{ kPa}, \\ c_u = 35.0\\text{ kPa}$, Soft</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(B) $q_u = 128.9\\text{ kPa}, \\ c_u = 64.4\\text{ kPa}$, Stiff</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(C) $q_u = 140.1\\text{ kPa}, \\ c_u = 70.0\\text{ kPa}$, Medium</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(D) $q_u = 128.9\\text{ kPa}, \\ c_u = 128.9\\text{ kPa}$, Stiff</div>\n</div>",
                "solution": "<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 1: Calculate Axial Strain ($epsilon$) and Corrected Area ($A_{\\text{corr}}$)</strong></p>\n$$\\epsilon = \\frac{\\Delta L}{L_0} = \\frac{8.0\\text{ mm}}{100.0\\text{ mm}} = 0.080$$\n$$A_0 = \\frac{\\pi D_0^2}{4} = \\frac{\\pi (0.050\\text{ m})^2}{4} = 1.9635 \\times 10^{-3}\\text{ m}^2$$\n$$A_{\\text{corr}} = \\frac{A_0}{1 - \\epsilon} = \\frac{1.9635 \\times 10^{-3}\\text{ m}^2}{1 - 0.080} = \\frac{1.9635 \\times 10^{-3}}{0.920} = 2.1342 \\times 10^{-3}\\text{ m}^2$$\n<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 2: Determine Unconfined Compressive Strength ($q_u$)</strong></p>\n$$q_u = \\frac{P_{\\max}}{A_{\\text{corr}}} = \\frac{275\\text{ N}}{2.1342 \\times 10^{-3}\\text{ m}^2} = 128{,}854\\text{ Pa} \\approx 128.9\\text{ kPa}$$\n<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 3: Calculate Undrained Cohesion ($c_u$) and Classify Consistency</strong></p>\n$$c_u = \\frac{q_u}{2} = \\frac{128.85\\text{ kPa}}{2} = 64.43\\text{ kPa} \\approx 64.4\\text{ kPa}$$\n<p>Since $100\\text{ kPa} \\le q_u < 200\\text{ kPa}$ (or $50\\text{ kPa} \\le c_u < 100\\text{ kPa}$), the clay is categorized as <strong>Stiff</strong>.</p>\n<p class=\"mt-2 pt-2 border-t border-emerald-500/20\"><strong class=\"text-cyan-300\">Correct Answer:</strong> <span class=\"text-emerald-300 font-bold\">(B) $q_u = 128.9\\text{ kPa}, \\ c_u = 64.4\\text{ kPa}$, Stiff</span></p>\n<p class=\"text-[11px] text-slate-400\"><em>FE Exam Tip:</em> If uncorrected area $A_0$ were mistakenly used, $q_u$ would be $275 / 0.0019635 = 140.1\\text{ kPa}$ (Option C). Always apply the area correction $A = A_0 / (1 - \\epsilon)$ when axial deformation is provided!</p>"
            }
