            "videoDuration": "10s",
            "solvedExample": {
                "question": "<p>A geotechnical rock coring barrel recovers an $N$-size core run of total length $L_{\\text{run}} = 1.50\\text{ m}$ ($150\\text{ cm}$) from a foundation exploratory borehole.</p>\n<p>The recovered sound, hard cylindrical rock core pieces have the following measured lengths:</p>\n<p>$7\\text{ cm}, \\ 14\\text{ cm}, \\ 22\\text{ cm}, \\ 8\\text{ cm}, \\ 18\\text{ cm}, \\ 31\\text{ cm}, \\ 5\\text{ cm}, \\ 12\\text{ cm}$, and $15\\text{ cm}$ of fragmented gravel-sized rubble.</p>\n<p>The Rock Quality Designation ($RQD$) and qualitative engineering rock classification are:</p>\n<div class=\"grid grid-cols-2 gap-2 my-2 font-mono text-xs\">\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(A) $RQD = 54.7\\%, \\$ Fair Quality</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(B) $RQD = 64.7\\%, \\$ Fair Quality</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(C) $RQD = 78.0\\%, \\$ Good Quality</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(D) $RQD = 88.0\\%, \\$ Good Quality</div>\n</div>",
                "solution": "<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 1: Identify Eligible Core Pieces ($\\ge 10\\text{ cm}$)</strong></p>\n<p>By ASTM D6032 standard, only sound core pieces with length $\\ge 10\\text{ cm}$ ($100\\text{ mm}$) are summed:</p>\n<p>• $7\\text{ cm}$: $< 10\\text{ cm}$ (Exclude)<br>\n• $14\\text{ cm}$: $\\ge 10\\text{ cm}$ (<strong>Include</strong>)<br>\n• $22\\text{ cm}$: $\\ge 10\\text{ cm}$ (<strong>Include</strong>)<br>\n• $8\\text{ cm}$: $< 10\\text{ cm}$ (Exclude)<br>\n• $18\\text{ cm}$: $\\ge 10\\text{ cm}$ (<strong>Include</strong>)<br>\n• $31\\text{ cm}$: $\\ge 10\\text{ cm}$ (<strong>Include</strong>)<br>\n• $5\\text{ cm}$: $< 10\\text{ cm}$ (Exclude)<br>\n• $12\\text{ cm}$: $\\ge 10\\text{ cm}$ (<strong>Include</strong>)<br>\n• Rubble: (Exclude)</p>\n<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 2: Sum Eligible Lengths</strong></p>\n$$\\sum L_{\\ge 10\\text{ cm}} = 14 + 22 + 18 + 31 + 12 = 97.0\\text{ cm}$$\n<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 3: Calculate $RQD$ Percentage</strong></p>\n$$RQD = \\frac{\\sum L_{\\ge 10\\text{ cm}}}{L_{\\text{total}}} \\times 100\\% = \\frac{97.0\\text{ cm}}{150.0\\text{ cm}} \\times 100\\% = 64.67\\% \\approx 64.7\\%$$\n<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 4: Engineering Classification</strong></p>\n<p>Because $50\\% \\le RQD = 64.7\\% < 75\\%$, the rock mass is classified as <strong>Fair Quality</strong>.</p>\n<p class=\"mt-2 pt-2 border-t border-emerald-500/20\"><strong class=\"text-cyan-300\">Correct Answer:</strong> <span class=\"text-emerald-300 font-bold\">(B) $RQD = 64.7\\%, \\$ Fair Quality</span></p>\n<p class=\"text-[11px] text-slate-400\"><em>FE Exam Tip:</em> If all core pieces including those $< 10\\text{ cm}$ were mistakenly summed, total recovery would be $117/150 = 78\\%$ (Option C). Remember that $RQD$ only awards credit to intact sound pieces of at least $10\\text{ cm}$ ($4\\text{ inches}$).</p>"
            }
