            "videoTitle": "Cascade Control Architecture for Secondary Disturbance Rejection Explainer",
            "videoDuration": "10s",
            "solvedExample": {
                "question": "<p>A jacketed chemical reactor uses cascade control to regulate reactor temperature ($T_1$, primary) by manipulating fuel flow rate ($F_2$, secondary) through a control valve.</p>\n<p>A disturbance $D_2$ represents an abrupt supply line gas pressure fluctuation directly affecting fuel flow.</p>\n<p>Inner loop parameters: slave controller proportional gain $K_{c2} = 8.0$, fuel valve/flow gain $K_{p2} = 1.25$.</p>\n<p>By what factor is the magnitude of the steady-state fuel disturbance effect attenuated by closing the inner secondary loop before it affects reactor temperature?</p>\n<div class=\"grid grid-cols-2 gap-2 my-2 font-mono text-xs\">\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(A) Disturbance reduced by a factor of $11.0$ ($90.9\\%$ attenuation)</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(B) Disturbance reduced by a factor of $8.0$ ($87.5\\%$ attenuation)</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(C) Disturbance reduced by a factor of $1.25$ ($20.0\\%$ attenuation)</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(D) Disturbance is unaffected by the inner loop</div>\n</div>",
                "solution": "<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 1: Set Up Secondary Closed-Loop Disturbance Transfer Function</strong></p>\n<p>In standard block diagram algebra, the response of secondary output $Y_2$ to an internal disturbance $D_2$ entering between controller and process is:</p>\n$$\\frac{Y_2(s)}{D_2(s)} = \\frac{1}{1 + G_{c2}(s) G_{p2}(s)}$$\n<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 2: Evaluate Steady-State Attenuation Factor</strong></p>\n$$\\text{Loop Gain } L_2(0) = K_{c2} \\times K_{p2} = 8.0 \\times 1.25 = 10.0$$\n$$\\text{Attenuation Factor} = \\frac{1}{1 + L_2(0)} = \\frac{1}{1 + 10.0} = \\frac{1}{11.0} = 0.0909$$\n<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 3: Quantify Disturbance Suppression</strong></p>\n$$\\text{Suppression} = (1 - 0.0909) \\times 100\\% = 90.91\\%$$\n<p class=\"mt-2 pt-2 border-t border-emerald-500/20\"><strong class=\"text-cyan-300\">Correct Answer:</strong> <span class=\"text-emerald-300 font-bold\">(A) Disturbance reduced by a factor of $11.0$ ($90.9\\%$ attenuation)</span></p>\n<p class=\"text-[11px] text-slate-400\"><em>FE Exam Tip:</em> In single-loop control without the inner slave loop, the full fuel pressure spike would propagate into the reactor before the slow temperature sensor could respond.</p>"
            }
