                "question": "<p>A quality audit records the daily machine shutdown scrap count $X$ with the following discrete probability distribution:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>$X = 0$ with $P(X = 0) = 0.50$</li>\n  <li>$X = 1$ with $P(X = 1) = 0.30$</li>\n  <li>$X = 2$ with $P(X = 2) = 0.15$</li>\n  <li>$X = 3$ with $P(X = 3) = 0.05$</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The expected daily scrap count $E[X]$ is:</p>\n<div class=\"grid grid-cols-2 gap-2 my-2 font-mono text-xs\">\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(A) $0.50$</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(B) $0.75$</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(C) $1.00$</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(D) $1.50$</div>\n</div>",
                "solution": "<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 1: Expected Value Formula for Discrete Variable</strong></p>\n$$E[X] = \\mu = \\sum_{i=1}^n x_i P(X = x_i)$$\n<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 2: Multiply Values by Probabilities</strong></p>\n$$E[X] = 0(0.50) + 1(0.30) + 2(0.15) + 3(0.05)$$\n$$E[X] = 0 + 0.30 + 0.30 + 0.15 = 0.75$$\n<p class=\"mt-2 pt-2 border-t border-emerald-500/20\"><strong class=\"text-cyan-300\">Correct Answer:</strong> <span class=\"text-emerald-300 font-bold\">(B) $0.75$</span></p>\n<p class=\"text-[11px] text-slate-400\"><em>FE Exam Tip:</em> Verify probabilities sum to 1: $0.50 + 0.30 + 0.15 + 0.05 = 1.00$. Expected value represents the long-run average outcome.</p>"
