            "videoDuration": "10s",
            "solvedExample": {
                "question": "<p>A 64-bit microprocessor has an on-chip $L1$ cache with hit latency $t_{L1} = 1.0\\text{ ns}$ (1 clock cycle) and hit rate $HR_{L1} = 94\\%$.</p>\n<p>Misses in $L1$ access an on-chip $L2$ cache with hit latency $t_{L2} = 5.0\\text{ ns}$ and local hit rate $HR_{L2} = 80\\%$.</p>\n<p>Misses in $L2$ access external main memory (DRAM), incurring a latency penalty of $t_{\\text{mem}} = 80.0\\text{ ns}$.</p>\n<p>The Average Memory Access Time ($AMAT$) of this memory hierarchy is most nearly:</p>\n<div class=\"grid grid-cols-2 gap-2 my-2 font-mono text-xs\">\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(A) $1.85\\text{ ns}$</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(B) $2.26\\text{ ns}$</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(C) $3.12\\text{ ns}$</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(D) $5.80\\text{ ns}$</div>\n</div>",
                "solution": "<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 1: Determine Cache Miss Rates ($MR$)</strong></p>\n$$MR_{L1} = 1 - HR_{L1} = 1 - 0.94 = 0.060 \\quad (6.0\\%$$\n$$MR_{L2} = 1 - HR_{L2} = 1 - 0.80 = 0.200 \\quad (20.0\\%$$\n<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 2: Calculate Effective $L1$ Miss Penalty via $L2$ Hierarchy</strong></p>\n$$t_{\\text{miss, } L1} = t_{L2} + MR_{L2} \\times t_{\\text{mem}} = 5.0\\text{ ns} + (0.20 \\times 80.0\\text{ ns}) = 5.0 + 16.0 = 21.0\\text{ ns}$$\n<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 3: Calculate Total Average Memory Access Time ($AMAT$)</strong></p>\n$$AMAT = t_{L1} + MR_{L1} \\times t_{\\text{miss, } L1} = 1.0\\text{ ns} + (0.060 \\times 21.0\\text{ ns}) = 1.0 + 1.26 = 2.26\\text{ ns}$$\n<p class=\"mt-2 pt-2 border-t border-emerald-500/20\"><strong class=\"text-cyan-300\">Correct Answer:</strong> <span class=\"text-emerald-300 font-bold\">(B) $2.26\\text{ ns}$</span></p>\n<p class=\"text-[11px] text-slate-400\"><em>FE Exam Tip:</em> Without the $L1$ and $L2$ caches, memory access would average $80\\text{ ns}$. The multi-level cache cuts latency to $2.26\\text{ ns}$—a $35\\times$ speedup!</p>"
            }
