            "videoDuration": "10s",
            "solvedExample": {
                "question": "<p>A water treatment plant rapid mix basin has volume $V = 8.0\\text{ m}^3$ treating flow $Q = 14{,}400\\text{ m}^3/\\text{day}$ ($0.1667\\text{ m}^3/\\text{s}$).</p>\n<p>Water temperature is $20^\\circ\\text{C}$ (dynamic viscosity $\\mu = 1.00 \\times 10^{-3}\\text{ Pa}\\cdot\\text{s}$). The mechanical mixer motor has wire-to-water efficiency $\\eta = 80.0\\%$.</p>\n<p>To establish a target velocity gradient $G = 800\\text{ s}^{-1}$, the hydraulic detention time ($t_d$), net mixing power ($P$), and required electric motor power input ($P_{\\text{motor}}$) are:</p>\n<div class=\"grid grid-cols-2 gap-2 my-2 font-mono text-xs\">\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(A) $t_d = 48.0\\text{ s}, \\ P = 5.12\\text{ kW}, \\ P_{\\text{motor}} = 6.40\\text{ kW}$</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(B) $t_d = 48.0\\text{ s}, \\ P = 6.40\\text{ kW}, \\ P_{\\text{motor}} = 8.00\\text{ kW}$</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(C) $t_d = 30.0\\text{ s}, \\ P = 5.12\\text{ kW}, \\ P_{\\text{motor}} = 6.40\\text{ kW}$</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(D) $t_d = 48.0\\text{ s}, \\ P = 5.12\\text{ kW}, \\ P_{\\text{motor}} = 4.10\\text{ kW}$</div>\n</div>",
                "solution": "<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 1: Calculate Hydraulic Detention Time ($t_d$)</strong></p>\n$$t_d = \\frac{V}{Q} = \\frac{8.0\\text{ m}^3}{0.16667\\text{ m}^3/\\text{s}} = 48.0\\text{ s}$$\n$$\\text{Camp Number } G t_d = (800\\text{ s}^{-1})(48.0\\text{ s}) = 38{,}400 \\quad (\\text{standard rapid mix: } 20{,}000\\text{--}50{,}000)$$\n<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 2: Calculate Power Dissipated into Water ($P$)</strong></p>\n$$P = G^2 \\mu V = (800\\text{ s}^{-1})^2 \\times (1.00 \\times 10^{-3}\\text{ Pa}\\cdot\\text{s}) \\times 8.0\\text{ m}^3$$\n$$P = 640{,}000 \\times 1.00 \\times 10^{-3} \\times 8.0 = 5{,}120\\text{ W} = 5.12\\text{ kW}$$\n<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 3: Calculate Motor Electric Power Input ($P_{\\text{motor}}$)</strong></p>\n$$P_{\\text{motor}} = \\frac{P}{\\eta} = \\frac{5.12\\text{ kW}}{0.80} = 6.40\\text{ kW} \\quad (8.58\\text{ HP})$$\n<p class=\"mt-2 pt-2 border-t border-emerald-500/20\"><strong class=\"text-cyan-300\">Correct Answer:</strong> <span class=\"text-emerald-300 font-bold\">(A) $t_d = 48.0\\text{ s}, \\ P = 5.12\\text{ kW}, \\ P_{\\text{motor}} = 6.40\\text{ kW}$</span></p>\n<p class=\"text-[11px] text-slate-400\"><em>FE Exam Tip:</em> Multiplying by efficiency instead of dividing ($5.12 \\times 0.80 = 4.10\\text{ kW}$, Option D) is a common trap. Electrical input must exceed water dissipation to overcome mechanical losses.</p>"
            }
