                "solution": "<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 1: Compute Capacity Scaling Factor</strong></p>\n$$\\frac{S_B}{S_A} = \\frac{45{,}000\\text{ gal}}{15{,}000\\text{ gal}} = 3.0$$\n$$\\left(\\frac{S_B}{S_A}\\right)^{0.60} = (3.0)^{0.60} \\approx 1.9332$$\n<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 2: Compute Cost Index Escalation Ratio</strong></p>\n$$\\frac{I_{2026}}{I_{2020}} = \\frac{810}{600} = 1.350$$\n<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 3: Calculate Estimated Capital Cost ($C_{B, 2026}$)</strong></p>\n$$C_{B, 2026} = C_{A, 2020} \\times \\left(\\frac{S_B}{S_A}\\right)^{0.60} \\times \\left(\\frac{I_{2026}}{I_{2020}}\\right)$$\n$$C_{B, 2026} = \\$180{,}000 \\times 1.9332 \\times 1.350 = \\$347{,}976 \\times 1.350 = \\$469{,}768 \\approx \\$470{,}000$$\n<p class=\"mt-2 pt-2 border-t border-emerald-500/20\"><strong class=\"text-cyan-300\">Correct Answer:</strong> <span class=\"text-emerald-300 font-bold\">(B) $\\$470{,}000$</span></p>\n<p class=\"text-[11px] text-slate-400\"><em>FE Exam Tip:</em> Option (A) $\\$348{,}000$ accounts only for capacity scaling without index escalation. Option (C) $\\$540{,}000$ uses linear 3× scaling without economics of scale. Option (D) combines linear scaling with inflation. The six-tenths rule reflects that costs grow sublinearly with volume ($3.0^{0.6} = 1.933 < 3.0$).</p>"
