            "description": "In statistical hypothesis testing, decision errors are classified into two fundamental types: (1) Type I Error ($\\alpha$, Significance Level / Producer's Risk): rejecting a true null hypothesis $H_0$ (false positive alarm). (2) Type II Error ($\\beta$, Consumer's Risk): failing to reject a false null hypothesis $H_0$ (false negative / missed detection). The statistical power of a test ($1 - \\beta$) is the probability of correctly rejecting a false null hypothesis. For a fixed sample size $n$, lowering $\\alpha$ increases $\\beta$. The only method to simultaneously reduce both $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ is to increase sample size $n$.",
