            "videoUrl": "assets/videos/Water_Chlorination_Breakpoint_Curve_and_Free_vs_Combined_Residuals.mp4",
            "videoTitle": "Water Chlorination Breakpoint Curve Explainer",
            "videoDuration": "10s",
            "solvedExample": {
                "question": "<p>A drinking water treatment plant operator performs a DPD spectrophotometric chlorine residual test on a finished water sample leaving the contact basin:</p>\n<p>• DPD-1 test (Free Available Chlorine): reading $= 1.80\\text{ mg/L}$<br>\n• DPD-4 test (Total Chlorine): reading $= 2.45\\text{ mg/L}$</p>\n<p>If the initial chlorine dosage injected into the water was $6.20\\text{ mg/L}$, calculate: (1) Combined chlorine residual, (2) Total chlorine demand of the water, and (3) verify if chlorination has passed the breakpoint.</p>\n<div class=\"grid grid-cols-2 gap-2 my-2 font-mono text-xs\">\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(A) Combined $= 0.65\\text{ mg/L}, \\ \\text{Demand} = 3.75\\text{ mg/L}$, Past Breakpoint</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(B) Combined $= 0.65\\text{ mg/L}, \\ \\text{Demand} = 4.40\\text{ mg/L}$, Before Breakpoint</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(C) Combined $= 1.80\\text{ mg/L}, \\ \\text{Demand} = 3.75\\text{ mg/L}$, At Breakpoint</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(D) Combined $= 0.45\\text{ mg/L}, \\ \\text{Demand} = 3.95\\text{ mg/L}$, Past Breakpoint</div>\n</div>",
                "solution": "<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 1: Calculate Combined Chlorine Residual</strong></p>\n$$\\text{Combined Residual} = \\text{Total Chlorine} - \\text{Free Chlorine} = 2.45\\text{ mg/L} - 1.80\\text{ mg/L} = 0.65\\text{ mg/L}$$\n<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 2: Calculate Total Chlorine Demand</strong></p>\n$$\\text{Chlorine Demand} = \\text{Chlorine Dose} - \\text{Total Residual} = 6.20\\text{ mg/L} - 2.45\\text{ mg/L} = 3.75\\text{ mg/L}$$\n<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 3: Verify Breakpoint Status</strong></p>\n<p>Because free available chlorine residual is substantial ($1.80\\text{ mg/L} > 0$), all ammonia and reducing agents have been completely oxidized. The system is operating in Zone 4 (past the breakpoint).</p>\n<p class=\"mt-2 pt-2 border-t border-emerald-500/20\"><strong class=\"text-cyan-300\">Correct Answer:</strong> <span class=\"text-emerald-300 font-bold\">(A) Combined $= 0.65\\text{ mg/L}, \\ \\text{Demand} = 3.75\\text{ mg/L}$, Past Breakpoint</span></p>\n<p class=\"text-[11px] text-slate-400\"><em>FE Exam Tip:</em> The presence of free available chlorine ($\\[\\text{HOCl}\\] + \\[\\text{OCl}^-\\]$) confirms that the breakpoint has been passed. In Zone 2 prior to the breakpoint, only combined residual exists.</p>"
            }
