            "description": "Hydraulic Retention Time ($\\theta$ or HRT), also called detention time or theoretical residence time, is the average time a fluid element spends inside an environmental treatment reactor, tank, or basin. It is defined as the active liquid volume $V$ divided by the influent volumetric flow rate $Q$ ($\\theta = V/Q$). For steady-state plug-flow basins, HRT determines the reaction duration available for biological organic oxidation, chemical coagulation/disinfection contact, or gravitational solids separation.",
