                "solution": "<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 1: Compute Clarifier Active Volume ($V$)</strong></p>\n$$V = L \\times W \\times H = 30.0\\text{ m} \\times 10.0\\text{ m} \\times 4.0\\text{ m} = 1200\\text{ m}^3$$\n<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 2: Convert Daily Flow Rate to Hourly Flow Rate ($Q$)</strong></p>\n$$Q = \\frac{14{,}400\\text{ m}^3/\\text{day}}{24\\text{ hours/day}} = 600\\text{ m}^3/\\text{hour}$$\n<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 3: Calculate Hydraulic Retention Time ($\\theta$)</strong></p>\n$$\\theta = \\frac{V}{Q} = \\frac{1200\\text{ m}^3}{600\\text{ m}^3/\\text{hour}} = 2.0\\text{ hours}$$\n<p class=\"mt-2 pt-2 border-t border-emerald-500/20\"><strong class=\"text-cyan-300\">Correct Answer:</strong> <span class=\"text-emerald-300 font-bold\">(B) $2.0\\text{ hours}$</span></p>\n<p class=\"text-[11px] text-slate-400\"><em>FE Exam Tip:</em> Primary clarifier detention times typically range from $1.5$ to $2.5\\text{ hours}$. A result outside this envelope often flags a unit conversion error.</p>"
