                "question": "<p>A regional municipal solid waste landfill cell receives a single placement of $M = 250{,}000\\text{ metric tons}$ ($\\text{Mg}$) of waste in a humid climate.</p>\n<p>Site-specific LandGEM modeling parameters:</p>\n<p>• Methane generation potential: $L_0 = 100\\text{ m}^3\\text{/Mg}$<br>\n• Methane decay rate constant: $k = 0.040\\text{ year}^{-1}$<br>\n• Landfill gas volumetric composition: $50\\% \\text{ CH}_4, \\ 50\\% \\text{ CO}_2$</p>\n<p>At $t = 5.0\\text{ years}$ following waste disposal, the annual methane generation rate ($Q_{CH_4}$) and total landfill gas generation rate ($Q_{\\text{LFG}}$) are most nearly:</p>\n<div class=\"grid grid-cols-2 gap-2 my-2 font-mono text-xs\">\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(A) $Q_{CH_4} = 410{,}000\\text{ m}^3\\text{/yr}, \\ Q_{\\text{LFG}} = 820{,}000\\text{ m}^3\\text{/yr}$</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(B) $Q_{CH_4} = 819{,}000\\text{ m}^3\\text{/yr}, \\ Q_{\\text{LFG}} = 1{,}637{,}000\\text{ m}^3\\text{/yr}$</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(C) $Q_{CH_4} = 1{,}000{,}000\\text{ m}^3\\text{/yr}, \\ Q_{\\text{LFG}} = 2{,}000{,}000\\text{ m}^3\\text{/yr}$</div>\n  <div class=\"p-2 bg-slate-900/80 rounded border border-slate-700/60\">(D) $Q_{CH_4} = 819{,}000\\text{ m}^3\\text{/yr}, \\ Q_{\\text{LFG}} = 819{,}000\\text{ m}^3\\text{/yr}$</div>\n</div>",
                "solution": "<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 1: Calculate Initial Generation Factor ($k L_0 M$)</strong></p>\n$$k L_0 M = (0.040\\text{ yr}^{-1}) \\times (100\\text{ m}^3\\text{/Mg}) \\times (250{,}000\\text{ Mg}) = 1{,}000{,}000\\text{ m}^3\\text{/year}$$\n<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 2: Compute Methane Generation at $t = 5.0\\text{ years}$</strong></p>\n$$Q_{CH_4}(5) = k L_0 M e^{-k t} = 1{,}000{,}000 \\times e^{-(0.040 \\times 5.0)} = 1{,}000{,}000 \\times e^{-0.20}$$\n$$e^{-0.20} = 0.81873 \\implies Q_{CH_4} = 1{,}000{,}000 \\times 0.81873 = 818{,}730\\text{ m}^3\\text{/year} \\approx 819{,}000\\text{ m}^3\\text{/year}$$\n<p><strong class=\"text-emerald-400\">Step 3: Calculate Total Landfill Gas Volume ($Q_{\\text{LFG}}$)</strong></p>\n<p>Because methane represents $50\\%$ of the raw gas mixture:</p>\n$$Q_{\\text{LFG}} = \\frac{Q_{CH_4}}{0.50} = 2 \\times 818{,}730 = 1{,}637{,}460\\text{ m}^3\\text{/year} \\approx 1{,}637{,}000\\text{ m}^3\\text{/year}$$\n<p class=\"mt-2 pt-2 border-t border-emerald-500/20\"><strong class=\"text-cyan-300\">Correct Answer:</strong> <span class=\"text-emerald-300 font-bold\">(B) $Q_{CH_4} = 819{,}000\\text{ m}^3\\text{/yr}, \\ Q_{\\text{LFG}} = 1{,}637{,}000\\text{ m}^3\\text{/yr}$</span></p>\n<p class=\"text-[11px] text-slate-400\"><em>FE Exam Tip:</em> Option (C) is the initial rate at $t=0$. For energy recovery systems, electricity generation potential is computed from the lower heating value of methane ($LHV_{CH_4} \\approx 37.7\\text{ MJ/m}^3$).</p>"
